  "oneLinerQuestion": "Find the minimum minutes required until no rotten orange is adjacent to a fresh one.",
  "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/rotting-oranges/",
  "explanation": "Multi-source Breadth-First Search (BFS): enqueue all initial rotten orange positions simultaneously, spreading rot step-by-step per minute level to adjacent fresh oranges.",
  "pseudoCode": "FUNCTION orangesRotting(grid):\n    q = Queue(), fresh = 0, time = 0\n    ROWS = LENGTH(grid), COLS = LENGTH(grid[0])\n    FOR r FROM 0 TO ROWS-1 DO:\n        FOR c FROM 0 TO COLS-1 DO:\n            IF grid[r][c] == 1 THEN fresh = fresh + 1\n            IF grid[r][c] == 2 THEN ENQUEUE(q, [r, c])\n        END FOR\n    END FOR\n    WHILE q AND fresh > 0 DO:\n        FOR i FROM 1 TO LENGTH(q) DO:\n            [r, c] = DEQUEUE(q)\n            FOR dr, dc IN [[1,0],[-1,0],[0,1],[0,-1]] DO:\n                row, col = r + dr, c + dc\n                IF row >= 0 AND row < ROWS AND col >= 0 AND col < COLS AND grid[row][col] == 1 THEN:\n                    grid[row][col] = 2; ENQUEUE(q, [row, col]); fresh = fresh - 1\n                END IF\n            END FOR\n        END FOR\n        time = time + 1\n    END WHILE\n    RETURN fresh == 0 ? time : -1\nEND FUNCTION",
